{"slug": "vietnamese-grilled-duck-salad-with-cucumber-radishes-and-peanuts", "nyt_id": 1013765, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013765-vietnamese-grilled-duck-salad-with-cucumber-radishes-and-peanuts", "name": "Vietnamese Grilled Duck Salad With Cucumber, Radishes and Peanuts", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "This zesty, cool and satisfying dish is worth making on any steamy summer night. The duck (you could use flank steak in a pinch, or for value) is marinated in a Vietnamese-inspired combination of soy sauce, lime, ginger, garlic, rice wine vinegar and fish sauce. The meat is grilled over indirect heat, and the result is meat beautifully infused with the flavors of the marinade. A crunchy slaw of cucumbers, radishes and carrots strewn with herbs and roasted peanuts finishes off the dish.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "PT40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "½ cup soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 limes", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "limes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons grated ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "grated ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons toasted (Asian) sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "toasted sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 garlic cloves, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 duck breast halves 2 ½ pounds, rinsed and patted dry", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "duck breast halves 2 ½ pounds", "preparation": "rinsed and patted dry", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 tablespoons rice wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "rice wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 teaspoons Thai or Vietnamese fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "thai or vietnamese fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "3 small jalapeños, seeded", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "small jalapeños", "preparation": "seeded", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup extra-virgin olive or peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive or peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 large cucumber, peeled and thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large cucumber", "preparation": "peeled and thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 large carrots, peeled and coarsely grated", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "large carrots", "preparation": "peeled and coarsely grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "⅓ pound radishes, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "lb", "item": "radishes", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "¼ cup chopped cilantro, plus more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": "plus more for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "¼ cup chopped mint, plus more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped mint", "preparation": "plus more for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "⅓ cup chopped salted roasted peanuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped salted roasted peanuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Whisk together ¼ cup soy sauce, juice and zest of 1 lime, ginger, and sesame oil. Mash half the garlic into a paste and whisk it into this marinade. Trim away the duck skin and most of the fat (reserve for rendering, if you like). Place the duck in a shallow dish and pour the marinade over it, turning to coat. Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for 1 to 12 hours. Remove from the refrigerator 30 minutes before cooking."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a small bowl, whisk together ¼ cup soy sauce, vinegar, juice of 2 limes, fish sauce, 2 jalapeños (finely chopped) and oil. Mash the remaining garlic to a paste and whisk into this vinaigrette."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Light a grill for high indirect heat (or heat a broiler with a rack 8 inches from the heat). Remove the duck from the marinade, scraping off any excess bits, and season with salt and pepper. Transfer duck to the unlighted portion of the grill; close cover and cook to desired doneness, 5 to 6 minutes per side for medium-rare. (If broiling, place duck on a baking sheet. Broil, turning once halfway through, 4 to 5 minutes per side for medium-rare.) Transfer to a cutting board and let it rest for 5 minutes. Thinly slice against the grain."}, {"position": 4, "text": "In a large bowl, toss together cucumber, carrots, radishes, cilantro, mint and 1 jalapeño (thinly sliced), with just enough of the vinaigrette to lightly coat everything. Taste and season with salt and pepper as needed. Toss in the peanuts. Place salad on a large platter and top with sliced meat. Drizzle with more of the vinaigrette, and sprinkle with cilantro and mint."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 494.0, "protein_g": 40.9, "carbohydrates_g": 19.8, "fat_g": 29.4, "saturated_fat_g": 5.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.4, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 127.8, "sodium_mg": 2128.1, "fiber_g": 5.8, "sugar_g": 5.8, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["vietnamese"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["carrot", "cucumber", "duck-breast", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/05/25/dining/25COOKINGweb2/25COOKINGweb2-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/05/25/dining/25COOKINGweb2/25COOKINGweb2-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/05/25/dining/25COOKINGweb2/25COOKINGweb2-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 121}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-08-03", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:45:54Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "vietnamese-pork-salad", "nyt_id": 1014080, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014080-vietnamese-pork-salad", "name": "Vietnamese Pork Salad", "author": "Laurie Woolever", "description": "Laurie Woolever", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 stalk lemon grass, very finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "stalk", "item": "lemon grass", "preparation": "very finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cloves garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 tablespoon brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 Thai chili, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "thai chili", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Four ½-inch-thick center-cut pork chops", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "four ½-inch-thick center-cut pork chops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 tablespoons fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 clove garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Half a small Thai chili, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "half a small thai chili", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 8-ounce package thin Vietnamese rice noodles", "group": null, "quantity": 9.0, "unit": null, "item": "ounce package thin vietnamese rice noodles", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 romaine hearts, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "romaine hearts", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Half a pomelo, or a small pink grapefruit, skin and membranes removed, shredded into small pieces", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "half a pomelo", "preparation": "or a small pink grapefruit, skin and membranes removed, shredded into small pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 large carrots, peeled and julienned", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "large carrots", "preparation": "peeled and julienned", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 cucumbers, peeled, seeded and julienned", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "cucumbers", "preparation": "peeled, seeded and julienned", "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "¼ cup chopped mint leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped mint leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "⅓ cup chopped cilantro leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped cilantro leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "½ cup chopped peanuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped peanuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "For the pork: In a large bowl, combine the lemon grass, garlic, brown sugar, fish sauce, chili and 1 tablespoon water. Add pork chops, turn to coat well, and let sit for at least 30 minutes or up to three hours."}, {"position": 2, "text": "For the dressing: In a small bowl, combine lime juice, fish sauce, garlic, chili and ½ cup water. Mix well. Dressing should be strong but not overwhelming; if desired, add up to ¼ cup more water."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat a grill or grill pan over high heat. Remove pork chops from marinade, brush off lemon grass and pat dry with paper towels. Place pork chops on grill or in pan and brown well, turning once, 2 to 3 minutes a side. Remove from heat and let rest about 5 minutes. Cut into thin slices and set aside."}, {"position": 4, "text": "For serving: Cook rice noodles according to package instructions and rinse under cold water. Drain, and mix in bowl with romaine, pomelo or grapefruit, carrots, cucumbers, mint and cilantro. Toss to mix. Add dressing and toss again. Top with pork and garnish with peanuts. Serve at room temperature."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 952.75, "protein_g": 57.1, "carbohydrates_g": 116.1, "fat_g": 28.3, "saturated_fat_g": 7.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.2, "cholesterol_mg": 137.3, "sodium_mg": 1773.9, "fiber_g": 8.7, "sugar_g": 11.5, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["vietnamese"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cucumber", "pork-chop", "quick", "rice-noodle"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 42}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-06-23", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:49:14Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "vietnamese-style-portobello-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 1013683, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013683-vietnamese-style-portobello-mushrooms", "name": "Vietnamese-Style Portobello Mushrooms", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "¼ cup peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ cup freshly squeezed lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "freshly squeezed lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh mint, plus more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh mint", "preparation": "plus more for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 fresh hot red chili like Thai, seeded and minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "fresh hot red chili like thai", "preparation": "seeded and minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ teaspoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "lots of black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "lots of black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "4 large portobello mushrooms, stems removed", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "large portobello mushrooms", "preparation": "stems removed", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat a charcoal or gas grill until quite hot and put the rack about 4 inches from the flame. Mix together the oil, lime juice, mint, chili, fish sauce and sugar and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Brush the mushrooms all over with about half of this mixture."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Grill the mushrooms with the tops of their caps away from the heat until they begin to brown, 5 to 8 minutes. Brush with the remaining marinade and turn. Grill until tender and nicely browned all over, 5 to 10 minutes more. Garnish with more mint and serve hot, warm or at room temperature."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 160.0, "protein_g": 3.2, "carbohydrates_g": 8.2, "fat_g": 14.0, "saturated_fat_g": 2.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.7, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 391.3, "fiber_g": 2.1, "sugar_g": 4.5, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["vietnamese"], "diet": [], "course": ["side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["lime-juice", "portobello", "quick", "summer", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/30/dining/Portobello-Mushrooms/Portobello-Mushrooms-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/30/dining/Portobello-Mushrooms/Portobello-Mushrooms-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 109}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-07-10", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:45:29Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "vietnamese-style-rice-noodle-and-steak-salad", "nyt_id": 1013190, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013190-vietnamese-style-rice-noodle-and-steak-salad", "name": "Vietnamese-Style Rice-Noodle and Steak Salad", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "Fish sauce and chilies play up the beefy nuances while peanuts add texture and a warm, toasted flavor to this Vietnamese-inspired cold steak and rice noodle salad. Use thin rice sticks to keep things as speedy as possible. They complement the flavors of the sauce and can be soaked instead of boiled.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 ounces (about ½ package) thin rice sticks (vermicelli)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "thin rice sticks", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 large garlic clove, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic clove", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 jalapeño, seeded and finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "jalapeño", "preparation": "seeded and finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 teaspoons granulated sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ cup fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 teaspoons freshly squeezed lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly squeezed lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup salted peanuts, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "salted peanuts", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 cup plus 1 tablespoon fresh mint leaves, torn into pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus 1 tablespoon fresh mint leaves", "preparation": "torn into pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 cup plus 1 tablespoon fresh basil leaves, torn into pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus 1 tablespoon fresh basil leaves", "preparation": "torn into pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "3 tablespoons peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 heads radicchio, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "head", "item": "radicchio", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ English cucumber, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": null, "item": "english cucumber", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "About ½ pound cooked steak, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "about ½ pound cooked steak", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh cilantro for garnish, optional", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh cilantro for garnish", "preparation": "optional", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the rice sticks in large bowl. Cover completely with boiling water and let stand until softened, about 10 minutes. Drain well."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a mortar and pestle (or small-capacity blender), mash the garlic, jalapeño and sugar to a paste. Transfer to a small bowl; whisk in the fish sauce, ¼ cup water and lime juice. Toss some of the dressing, a few tablespoons at a time, with the noodles, tasting as you go, until the flavor is to your liking; use up to half the dressing. Add 6 tablespoons nuts, 1 tablespoon mint and 1 tablespoon basil. Toss well."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Whisk the peanut oil into the remaining dressing. In a large bowl, toss together the radicchio, remaining 1 cup mint, remaining 1 cup basil and cucumber. Pour enough dressing over the salad to lightly coat the greens; reserve some dressing for the meat."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Arrange the salad on a large platter. Top with the noodles. Arrange the steak over the noodles and spoon additional dressing over the meat if desired. Garnish with the remaining 2 tablespoons peanuts and cilantro, if using."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 486.75, "protein_g": 20.6, "carbohydrates_g": 38.6, "fat_g": 28.7, "saturated_fat_g": 7.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.5, "cholesterol_mg": 35.2, "sodium_mg": 1581.3, "fiber_g": 4.6, "sugar_g": 7.0, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["asian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-pastas-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "quick", "steak", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/25/dining/steaksalad-still/steaksalad-still-superJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/25/dining/steaksalad-still/steaksalad-still-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 238}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-07-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:35:33Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
